.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt FFPROBE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ffprobe
.Nd report the streams and format of an audio file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar input
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads an audio file and reports its container and streams.
It is installed with FFmpeg in the GNU root and uses the same built-in
formats and decoders; see
.Xr ffmpeg 1 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl show_format
Print the container's properties, such as duration and bit rate.
.It Fl show_streams
Print each stream's codec, sample rate and channel count.
.It Fl show_entries Ar entries
Select the properties to print.
.It Fl of Ar format
Select an output format, such as
.Cm json
or
.Cm default .
.It Fl v Ar level
Set the logging level.
Use
.Cm error
to omit routine diagnostics.
.It Fl h
Print the command's help.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print the audio stream's codec, rate and channels as JSON:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ffprobe -v error -show_entries stream=codec_name,sample_rate,channels \
    -of json music.flac
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ffmpeg 1
